# Kept — AI working rules

Full canonical context lives in `AGENTS.md`. Follow it. Summary of hard constraints:

## Product
Receipt → OCR → structured purchase → SwiftData → Wallet pass + 14-day expiry notification → claim pack PDF. Countdown is the product, not filing. On-device privacy; only pass signing leaves the phone.

## Timeline
Shipaton 2026. App Store review submit **Sep 14**. Devpost closes Sep 30. Do not build ahead of the current milestone — say so and stop.

## Platform
- Minimum **iOS 26.0**
- Extraction is **two-tiered** behind `ExtractionService`: rules parser (all devices) + Foundation Models enrichment (Apple Intelligence only). Never gate core flows or upsell Apple Intelligence.
- Dev device is iPhone 13 — no on-device Foundation Models there.
- Pass signing is **off-device**. Never put the Pass Type ID private key in the app or repo.

## Stack
Swift 6 / SwiftUI / SwiftData / Vision / FoundationModels / PassKit / UserNotifications / RevenueCat (SPM). Swift Testing, not XCTest. **RevenueCat is the only third-party dependency** — ask before adding anything.

## Architecture
Flat feature folders. Views own no business logic. Services are protocol-backed and injectable. Every view needs a working `#Preview`. No singletons unless Apple forces one.

## Data model
`Purchase`, `WarrantyTerm`, `PassRecord`. CloudKit-shaped: defaults on all stored props, optional relationships, no `@Attribute(.unique)`. Warranties are **one-to-many**; `coverageEndsAt` denormalised on `Purchase` via `refreshCoverage()`. `WarrantySource` as raw String. User edits always win over inference. Ask before changing the schema.

## Design
HIG-native layout; motion is the signature. One accent color, SF Pro, Dynamic Type to XXL. Timing: task path <300ms; only two reward moments up to 900ms. Five motion files under `DesignSystem/Motion/`. No SceneKit, RealityKit, Lottie, or third-party design systems. Reduce Motion paths alongside every animation.

## Conventions
No force unwrap / `try!` outside tests. Typed errors, plain-language UI. Async/await only. Ask before new deps, data model changes, or architecture patterns. Smallest change that works. When a build fails, show the actual error first.
